# Build-context exclusions for the five images built from the repository root
# (trainer, post-training, serving, drift-monitor, data-gen). Docker reads this file from
# the context root, so it does not apply to the dbt image — that one builds from
# projects/dbt_transform/ and carries its own .dockerignore.
#
# Every root-context Dockerfile COPYs an explicit allowlist: the workspace manifest, the
# lockfile, and the pyproject.toml plus src/ of each package it depends on. Nothing listed
# here is ever copied into an image, so excluding it only cuts the context upload — which
# is the whole point, since the context is otherwise the entire monorepo.

# Local virtualenvs. The builder stage creates its own from uv.lock; shipping a host-built
# one would also mix macOS wheels into a Linux image.
.venv/
**/.venv/

.git/
.gitignore

# Python caches and coverage artefacts
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
*.egg-info/

# Test suites: images copy src/ only, and tests run as their own Cloud Build step.
**/tests/

# Terraform. .terraform/ vendors provider binaries (hundreds of MB) and local state files
# can contain secrets — neither belongs anywhere near an image build.
iac/

# Notebooks commit their rendered outputs deliberately (see docs/feature-exploration.md),
# which makes them large. They are exploration artefacts and are never deployed.
notebooks/

# The dbt project builds from its own context; its target/, dbt_packages/ and logs/
# directories are pure local build output.
projects/dbt_transform/

# Docs, CI definitions, deploy-time YAML and local tooling state
docs/
.cloudbuild/
.github/
*.md
.pre-commit-config.yaml
.serena/
.claude/
scripts/
workflows/
